<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vaud</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pays de Vaud, Canton of Vaud</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vaud is a French-speaking canton of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, stretching from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-geneva">Lake Geneva</a> to the Jura with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lausanne">Lausanne</a> as its capital. Long divided between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Lausanne and the house of Savoy, it was conquered by Bern in 1536 and ruled as a subject territory until the revolution of 1798. It became a full Swiss canton in 1803.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vaud.jpg" alt="Vaud" width="320" height="301" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tschubby · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karte_Kanton_Waadt_2010.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
